112
00:07:55.467 --> 00:07:56.626
(narrator) Verse 3, the iceberg.

113
00:07:56.626 --> 00:08:07.665
(narrator) The tip above the water is labeled interface, a stable contract; below, a yellow submarine’s sonar finds the implementation, where turning gears are swapped for new ones while the tip stays unchanged.

114
00:08:07.665 --> 00:08:13.682
(narrator) Below the waterline, three choice switches flip: array or hash table, cache or no cache, MongoDB or Supabase.

115
00:08:13.682 --> 00:08:21.133
(narrator) Then a cutaway wall: a phone charges from an outlet while, behind the wall, solar panels at noon give way to wind turbines at midnight.

116
00:08:21.133 --> 00:08:24.776
(narrator) The outlet is the interface; the power plant is the sealed secret.

117
00:08:25.373 --> 00:08:27.973
♪ Picture an iceberg. The tip’s the interface: ♪

118
00:08:27.973 --> 00:08:30.833
